@namespace DotNetCloud.Modules.Email.UI

@*
    Help content for the Email module.
*@

<div class="help-content">
    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Overview</h2>
        <p>DotNetCloud Email is a web-based email client. Add one or more email accounts (IMAP/SMTP or Gmail via OAuth), read and organize your messages, and compose and send email from your browser.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Accounts</h2>
        <p><strong>Adding an account:</strong> Click <strong>+ Account</strong> and choose <strong>IMAP / SMTP</strong> (enter your server, port, username, and password) or <strong>Gmail (OAuth)</strong> (if configured by your administrator).</p>
        <p><strong>Switching accounts:</strong> Use the account selector in the sidebar. Use <strong>Sync Now</strong> to fetch new messages, or <strong>Delete Account</strong> to remove an account and its synced messages.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Composing Messages</h2>
        <p>Click <strong>+ Compose</strong> to open the message editor. Pick the account to send from, enter the recipient(s) with optional <strong>Cc</strong> and <strong>Bcc</strong>, a subject, and the message body. Recipient suggestions appear as you type.</p>
        <p><strong>Attachments:</strong> Use <strong>Attach from computer</strong> to upload files, or <strong>Browse Files</strong> to attach files from your DotNetCloud Files library.</p>
        <p>Use <strong>Reply</strong> and <strong>Forward</strong> from an open message. Closing the compose window discards the draft.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Folders</h2>
        <p>The sidebar lists the mailboxes synced from your account (for example <strong>Inbox</strong>, <strong>Sent</strong>, <strong>Drafts</strong>, <strong>Spam</strong>, and <strong>Trash</strong>, depending on your server). Click a folder to view its message threads.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Reading Messages</h2>
        <p>Click a thread to open it. Attachments can be downloaded, and messages with stored attachments can be saved to your Files library with the folder button.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Rules</h2>
        <p>Automate how incoming messages are handled. Open <strong>Rules</strong> in the sidebar and create a rule with conditions (subject, from, to, body, cc, or has attachment) and actions (mark read or unread, star or unstar, apply a label, move to a folder, or archive). Rules run in priority order and can be enabled or disabled individually. Use <strong>Run Rules Now</strong> to apply rules to existing messages.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="help-section">
        <h2 class="help-section-title">Tips &amp; Tricks</h2>
        <ul class="help-tips">
            <li>Add multiple email accounts and switch between them with the account selector.</li>
            <li>Create rules to automatically organize incoming email into folders or labels.</li>
            <li>Attach files directly from your Files library with <strong>Browse Files</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
    </section>
</div>
